{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Cloud ADF codec — make the AdfCodec Markdown-aware (capability only; no live cutover)\n\n## Context / Problem\nJira Cloud stores rich text as ADF (structured JSON). The `RichTextCodec` seam\n(epic `e369`, story J3 / `aac8`) routes Cloud rich text through `AdfCodec`\n(`adapters/jira/rich_text_codec.py`), a pass-through wrapper over the pinned\n`adapters/jira/adf.py`. **`adf.py`'s encode is plain-text-structured, not\nMarkdown-aware:** `text_to_adf` (`adf.py:275`) splits the body on blank lines and\nemits each block as one `paragraph` node, so Markdown block syntax (headings,\nlist markers, fenced code) and inline syntax (`**bold**`, `~~strike~~`, `[t](url)`)\nis carried as **literal characters** and Cloud renders raw source. Its `adf_to_text`\n(`adf.py:26`) already emits Markdown-ish text on decode; the missing half is a\nMarkdown-aware **encode**.\n\n**Scope boundary (why this story changes nothing observable yet).** The live Cloud\noutbound send does **not** go through `AdfCodec` today — it calls `adf.py`\nfunctions **directly**: `_text_to_adf` = `adf.text_to_adf` at `acli.py:205` and\n`acli_cli_ops.py:369`, and the description-compare sites call\n`adf.normalize_description` / `adf.fit_text_to_adf_limit` directly at\n`outbound_fields.py:564` and `inbound_differ.py:210`. Therefore **repointing\n`AdfCodec` alone does not change the ADF that is posted to Cloud.** This story\ndelivers only the **codec capability** — a Markdown-aware, codec-law-consistent\n`AdfCodec` plus its unit/corpus tests. **Rerouting those live call sites through\nthe capable codec (the observable cutover), the second-pass convergence proof, and\nthe rollback path are owned by the echo-safety story `3388`, which depends on this\none** — so the safety layer lands *with* the cutover, never before it. Until\n`3388` wires it, `AdfCodec` is capable but inert and no already-synced body is\nre-emitted by this story.\n\n## Prior art in this repo (the seam we build on — NOT greenfield)\n- `RichTextCodec` Protocol — `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py` (four ops:\n  `fit_outbound`, `normalize_outbound`, `to_wire`, `decode_inbound`).\n- `AdfCodec` (Cloud) — `adapters/jira/rich_text_codec.py`; delegates each op to\n  `adf.py`. Pinned as a wrapper (not a copy) by `test_rich_text_codec.py`:\n  `test_adf_codec_is_a_pass_through_to_the_pinned_adf_module` (`:198`) asserting\n  `fit_outbound == adf.fit_text_to_adf_limit` (`:205`), `to_wire == adf.text_to_adf`\n  (`:207`), and `decode_inbound == adf.adf_to_text(...)` (`:208`). **These are the\n  exact pin tests this story updates.**\n- `adf.py` — `text_to_adf` (`:275`), `adf_to_text` (`:26`), `normalize_description`\n  (`:310` = `adf_to_text(text_to_adf(text))`), `fit_text_to_adf_limit` (`:341`).\n- `OutboundFieldMapper` — `adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py:77` composes\n  `normalize_outbound(fit_outbound(value))` for the description (a **compare/render\n  op**, not the live encode — the live Cloud encode is the direct `adf.py` calls\n  named above).\n\n## Engine decision: vendored `marklas` (committed, not a spike)\nUse **`marklas`** (pure-Python, mistune-based, MIT) for Markdown↔ADF, **vendored\nunder `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/` with its upstream provenance recorded**:\n- Upstream: `https://github.com/byExist/marklas`; PyPI distribution `marklas`.\n- Pin the exact upstream **version + commit sha in `pyproject.toml`**, and copy the\n  upstream **MIT `LICENSE`** into `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/LICENSE` (single-\n  maintainer bus-factor is mitigated by vendoring a pinned copy).\n\nThis is a **committed decision backed by a completed experiment**, not an open\nspike: a direct head-to-head against `adf.py` over the **live store corpus\n(`rebar export`, 5,730 bodies, 2026-08-03)** measured marklas at **99.65%\nidempotent round-trip** (echo-safe under the reconciler's normalize-both-sides\nmodel) while producing **structurally-rich ADF for 56.7%** of bodies (56.3% both\nrich AND idempotent). The ≥99.6% AC below locks that measured bar in as a\nregression. Scripts + raw counts: session log `5eb0-52a3-45f0-43e5`;\n`files/parity_*.py`, `files/parity-results.md`.\n\n### Rejected alternative — extend `adf.py`'s handlers in-house\nWeighed and **rejected on empirical grounds** (recorded here so the review sees the\nrationale). The appeal was that `adf.py`'s *decode* already emits Markdown-ish\ntext, suggesting a symmetric *encode* is small. The live-corpus head-to-head\nrefutes this for the half that matters — the **encode**:\n- `adf.py`'s `text_to_adf` produces **0%** structurally-rich ADF over the 5,730\n  bodies: it flattens **every** construct to paragraph text and emits **zero** ADF\n  marks. Of the bodies marklas renders as structured ADF, `adf.py` renders **0**:\n  headings (1,924), bullet lists (2,538), task lists (1,780), ordered lists (795),\n  code blocks (280), tables (60), blockquotes (33), rules (72); inline marks strong\n  (1,396), inline-code (2,569), em (439), strike (7), link (12) — all 0.\n- `adf.py`'s 100% round-trip fidelity is therefore **trivial**: it translates no\n  rich structure, so there is nothing to lose. It is a plain-text→paragraph\n  encoder, not a Markdown↔ADF codec.\n- Reaching marklas parity in-house means building a **full GFM→ADF parser + ADF→GFM\n  serializer** — i.e. re-implementing marklas/mistune. The prior hand-rolled\n  attempt stalled at **90.7%** fixed point, its residual tail being exactly the\n  emphasis/mark serialization a bespoke engine gets wrong. Only the *decode* half\n  overlaps; the *encode* is greenfield.\n\n## Approach (capability, behind the seam)\n1. **Add Markdown-aware `markdown_to_adf` / `adf_to_markdown` /\n   `fit_markdown_to_adf_limit` in `adf.py`** (thin wrappers over vendored marklas),\n   keeping plain `text_to_adf` / `adf_to_text` / `normalize_description` /\n   `fit_text_to_adf_limit` intact for the fallback and the shared/plain callers.\n2. **Repoint ALL FOUR `AdfCodec` ops together** (consistency is load-bearing for\n   the codec law): `to_wire`→`markdown_to_adf`, `decode_inbound`→`adf_to_markdown`,\n   `normalize_outbound`→`adf_to_markdown(markdown_to_adf(text))`, and\n   `fit_outbound`→`fit_markdown_to_adf_limit` (the old `fit_text_to_adf_limit`\n   measured the plain encode, so it must be repointed or it no longer bounds the\n   real wire). No partial repoint.\n3. **Codec-law invariant.** The four ops must satisfy the pinned parametrized law\n   `normalize_outbound(t) == decode_inbound(to_wire(t))` in\n   `test_rich_text_codec.py`. A deterministic mark-order canonicalizer is applied\n   **identically** inside `to_wire`'s decode-preview, `decode_inbound`, and\n   `normalize_outbound`, so the law holds for Markdown fixtures too.\n4. **Loop prevention within the codec.** Keep `normalize_outbound` as the\n   idempotent \"reads-after-round-trip\" transform. Fix the one true 2-cycle\n   oscillator — co-located `strong`+`strikethrough` (`**~~x~~**` ⇄ `~~**x~~**`, no\n   canonical mark order) — with the mark-order canonicalizer. Whitespace-only\n   transients converge under normalize-both-sides.\n5. **Failure path = WHOLE-CODEC degrade (preserves the law).** On any conversion\n   error for a field, degrade THAT field's codec to the plain path *consistently* —\n   `to_wire`→`adf.text_to_adf`, `decode_inbound`→`adf.adf_to_text`,\n   `normalize_outbound`→`adf.normalize_description`,\n   `fit_outbound`→`fit_text_to_adf_limit` **together** (never a mixed\n   Markdown/plain codec, which would break the law) — log the body id, continue.\n\n## Explicitly OUT of scope for this story (owned by `3388`)\n- Rerouting the live Cloud encode (`acli.py:205`, `acli_cli_ops.py:369`) and the\n  description-compare sites (`outbound_fields.py:564`, `inbound_differ.py:210`)\n  through `AdfCodec` — the observable wire cutover.\n- The already-synced-body re-emit migration (each stale body re-emitted once), the\n  second-pass convergence proof, and the rollback path.\n- Comment CREATE-path rendering through `to_wire` (story `789c` / cut over by\n  `3388`). This story leaves those direct `adf.py` call sites untouched, so no\n  observable Cloud behavior changes on merge.\n\n## Scope\n- `adapters/jira/adf.py` — add `markdown_to_adf` / `adf_to_markdown` /\n  `fit_markdown_to_adf_limit`; plain functions kept for fallback + shared callers.\n- `adapters/jira/rich_text_codec.py` — repoint all four `AdfCodec` ops + mark-order\n  canonicalizer; whole-codec fallback.\n- `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/` — vendored, sha-pinned copy + upstream `LICENSE`.\n- `pyproject.toml` — record the vendored upstream version + sha.\n- **Guard (UNCHANGED):** the shared plain-text `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text`\n  (ticket 21ca; also used by sibling repo `agentic-dev-platform`), and the live\n  send sites `acli.py:205` / `acli_cli_ops.py:369` / `outbound_fields.py:564` /\n  `inbound_differ.py:210` (rerouted later by `3388`).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_codec.py` — update the pin tests at\n  `:198`/`:205`/`:207`/`:208` to the Markdown-aware delegation.\n\n## Testing (unit + corpus only — no live send in this story)\n- **Pin test (updated):** `test_adf_codec_is_a_pass_through_to_the_pinned_adf_module`\n  asserts `to_wire is adf.markdown_to_adf`, `decode_inbound` maps to\n  `adf.adf_to_markdown`, and `fit_outbound is adf.fit_markdown_to_adf_limit`\n  (wrapper-not-a-copy preserved for all four ops).\n- **Codec law:** the parametrized `test_rich_text_codec` law\n  `normalize_outbound(t) == decode_inbound(to_wire(t))` holds over Markdown\n  fixtures (headings/lists/code-fence/combined-marks).\n- **Structured round trip:** heading+checklist+inline-code+link round-trips\n  MD→ADF→MD to a fixed point, asserting ADF node types (`test_cloud_adf_roundtrip`).\n- **Fit measures the real wire:** add\n  `test_adf_fit_measures_the_serialized_document_not_the_plain_text` asserting\n  `fit_outbound` bounds the `markdown_to_adf` serialization, not the plain encode.\n- **Oscillation:** the two known combined strong+strikethrough bodies converge in\n  ≤1 pass; a permutation property test asserts 100% convergence.\n- **Corpus idempotence:** the round-trip is idempotent (normalize-both-sides\n  stable, `r(r(x))==r(x)`) for ≥99.6% of the 5,730 live-store bodies\n  (`test_cloud_corpus_idempotence`; measured 99.65%).\n- **Whole-codec fallback:** an un-convertible body degrades the WHOLE codec for\n  that field to plain-text, the law still holds, and no test drives a live send\n  (`test_cloud_adf_conversion_fallback`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `marklas` is vendored under `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/` with its upstream\n  `github.com/byExist/marklas` version + commit sha recorded in `pyproject.toml`\n  and its MIT `LICENSE` copied alongside; verified by an import/provenance test\n  asserting the pinned sha and the presence of the MIT license text.\n- [ ] All four `AdfCodec` ops are Markdown-aware and delegate to `adf.py`\n  (`to_wire→markdown_to_adf`, `decode_inbound→adf_to_markdown`,\n  `normalize_outbound→adf_to_markdown∘markdown_to_adf`,\n  `fit_outbound→fit_markdown_to_adf_limit`); verified by the updated pin tests at\n  `test_rich_text_codec.py:198/205/207/208`.\n- [ ] `AdfCodec.to_wire` emits Markdown-aware ADF (heading/list/code/emphasis\n  nodes, not literal `#`/`-`/`**`) and `decode_inbound` returns the source\n  Markdown; verified by `test_cloud_adf_roundtrip` asserting node types and decoded\n  equality.\n- [ ] The codec law `normalize_outbound(t) == decode_inbound(to_wire(t))` holds\n  over Markdown fixtures; verified by the parametrized law test in\n  `test_rich_text_codec.py`.\n- [ ] `AdfCodec.fit_outbound` measures the `markdown_to_adf` serialization; verified\n  by `test_adf_fit_measures_the_serialized_document_not_the_plain_text`.\n- [ ] The combined strong+strikethrough oscillation is eliminated by a mark-order\n  canonicalizer applied identically in `to_wire`/`decode_inbound`/`normalize_outbound`;\n  verified by the regression + permutation property test (100% convergence).\n- [ ] The MD→ADF→MD round-trip is idempotent (normalize-both-sides stable) for\n  ≥99.6% of the 5,730 live-store bodies; verified by `test_cloud_corpus_idempotence`.\n- [ ] A conversion failure degrades the WHOLE codec for that field to plain-text\n  (law preserved) without aborting; verified by `test_cloud_adf_conversion_fallback`.\n- [ ] The shared `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text` and the live send sites\n  (`acli.py:205`, `acli_cli_ops.py:369`, `outbound_fields.py:564`,\n  `inbound_differ.py:210`) are unchanged by this story; verified by their existing\n  tests staying green (the observable cutover is `3388`)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785810332451628001,"uuid":"a212857a-d983-4894-8288-09d38f028796"}